# The varnamelen ignore list is a YAML flow sequence with comments grouping the
# names into three annotated categories -- which is how anyone adding a
# one-letter name knows where to put it. Prettier explodes a flow sequence to
# one entry per line, and the grouping stops meaning anything.
.golangci.yml

# Local scratch: .issues/ is written by the code-* skills, .planning/ by
# release-captain. Prettier reads this repo's .gitignore but not the global
# core.excludesfile, and both are ignored through the latter -- so git hides
# them and prettier would not. Without these lines the gate fails on files the
# repository does not carry.
.issues/
.planning/
